WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.495
Welcome to our training on return reports.

00:00:02.495 --> 00:00:05.702
It's wonderful when customers love the products they buy,

00:00:05.702 --> 00:00:11.761
but sometimes a customer opens a box to find that the product just isn't right for them.

00:00:11.761 --> 00:00:14.968
When that happens, they may decide to return it.

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:17.463
Keeping track of which products are returned

00:00:17.463 --> 00:00:20.671
and when is an important part of your business.

00:00:20.671 --> 00:00:23.878
You can use our return reports feature to monitor

00:00:23.878 --> 00:00:25.660
customer returns and generate records.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.953
To access your return reports, open the Seller Central Main

00:00:29.953 --> 00:00:33.116
menu, hover over Reports and click Return Reports.

00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:36.674
On the Return Reports page, you can track your

00:00:36.674 --> 00:00:43.000
history of returns by generating reports on demand or by scheduling them on a regular basis.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.571
Your first option is to generate a one-time report.

00:00:46.571 --> 00:00:49.071
To do this, start by selecting whether

00:00:49.071 --> 00:00:53.000
you'd like a report for all returns or only prime returns.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.395
Then select the time period that you'd

00:00:55.395 --> 00:00:57.105
like the report to cover.

00:00:57.105 --> 00:01:01.553
If you select exact dates, you'll then need to select the date range

00:01:01.553 --> 00:01:03.605
you want the report to cover.

00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:06.000
Once you've made your choices, select Request.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.455
Once you request a

00:01:07.455 --> 00:01:11.455
report, you'll see a notice that the report is in progress.

00:01:11.455 --> 00:01:13.636
Your request will appear under Generated

00:01:13.636 --> 00:01:14.000
Reports.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:20.652
How long it takes to create the report will depend on the number of returns in that report's

00:01:20.652 --> 00:01:21.391
date range.

00:01:21.391 --> 00:01:24.348
Select Refresh to check on the report's status.

00:01:24.348 --> 00:01:26.935
If there were returns during that period,

00:01:26.935 --> 00:01:31.000
you'll receive links to an XML file and a TSV file.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.294
XML stands for the Extensible Markup Language,

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:39.000
while a TSV file is a tab-separated values file.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.500
Most commercial spreadsheet applications can

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.000
open TSV files.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:49.000
If you want to schedule a regular report, select Schedule Report Generation.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.857
Here, you can generate three different types of reports.

00:01:52.857 --> 00:01:54.143
Reports for exemptions,

00:01:54.143 --> 00:01:58.000
reports for all returns, and reports for prime returns.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.450
Select how often you'd like to receive

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:05.000
any of the report choices, and then select Schedule next to that option.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.000
If you have a report scheduled,

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:12.667
you'll see the date when the next report will be generated, as well as options to reschedule

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:14.000
or unschedule a report.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.889
Rescheduling a report will change the report timing, while unscheduling

00:02:17.889 --> 00:02:21.000
a report stops it from being automatically generated.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.333
When a scheduled report is created,

00:02:23.333 --> 00:02:28.000
you can find it under generated reports on the return reports page.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.333
When you open a return report,

00:02:30.333 --> 00:02:35.000
you'll see information about every return that meets the criteria you chose.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.474
You can see the

00:02:36.474 --> 00:02:42.000
order ID, the order date, the date the return was requested, and the return status.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:42.938
The next set

00:02:42.938 --> 00:02:47.000
of columns provides information about the return label and how it was shipped.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.312
For more information

00:02:48.312 --> 00:02:54.000
about return labels, search for prepaid returns and returnless resolutions in Seller Central.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:59.409
You'll also find information about whether the return was the result of an A-Z guarantee claim,

00:02:59.409 --> 00:03:05.235
or was a prime order, as well as information about the product itself, how many were returned,

00:03:05.235 --> 00:03:07.000
and why they were returned.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:11.000
This information is important to helping you monitor your inventory.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:15.667
If you see many orders of the same product returned for the same reason,

00:03:15.667 --> 00:03:20.000
check your product and its listing to make sure there aren't any problems.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.000
You may be able to catch these before they impact your account health.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:29.000
The next set of columns show whether your return is related to SAFE-T claims.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:29.444
SAFE-T

00:03:29.444 --> 00:03:33.000
stands for Seller Assurance for E-Commerce Transactions.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.000
A seller might make a SAFE-T claim if Amazon

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:41.333
processes a return on the seller's behalf, but certain conditions are met that show the seller

00:03:41.333 --> 00:03:43.000
isn't responsible for the return.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:47.375
To learn more about SAFE-T claims, search for "SAFE-T claim"

00:03:47.375 --> 00:03:50.000
in the Seller Central search bar.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:53.125
In the very last column, you can see the amount

00:03:53.125 --> 00:03:55.000
refunded to customers for each return.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.889
If you sell products using fulfillment by Amazon or FBA,

00:03:58.889 --> 00:04:02.000
there are other reports specific to FBA sellers.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:06.200
To access them, click "View FBA Reports" near the

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:09.000
top of the return reports page.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:12.000
This concludes our training on return reports.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.000
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store.
